00408 14.8432L4.40172 22.6166C4.35092 22.7683 4.37534 22.9352 4.46749 23.066C4.6275 23.2932 4.94137 23.3476 5.16853 23.1876L12 18.3758L18.8317 23.183C18.9625 23.2751 19.1293 23.2994 19.281 23.2486C19.5445 23.1604 19.6865 22.8752 19.5983 22.6117L16.996 14.8432L23.7872 10.0456C23.9206 9.95133 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></defs><use clip-path="url(#clip_RatingStar_undefined-1small)" href="#path_RatingStar_undefined-1small" class="RatingStar__backgroundFill"></use><path class="RatingStar__fill"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/2392373040">May 15, 2018</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">Unravelling Darkness picks up immediately where Tracing Shadows ended, with our intrepid band travelling to Everett to seek shelter. As in the previous book, world-building is rather narrow, but the same certainly can't be said of the relationships - they, and the dash of romance, progress organically and believably. <br /><br />I admit that I skimmed over most of the crystal and magic stuff because I just wasn't that interested, but that may well be just a 'me' issue. I also had to knock a star off because of Violet - no spoilers, but I felt so, so sorry for her! I do think the other characters, especially her own brother, ought to have shown a modicum more concern for her rather than just writing her off like that. <br /><br />Overall, a solid read with 4/5 stars for characters and 3 for plot. 3.5, here we come! </span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/31792110?shelf=arc" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Bu