dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">I can't believe it's done. This book was everything I hoped it would be. It was fast paced and thrilling with just the right amount of swoon to make my knees go weak. I took my time and savored every page. I didn't want it to end. I wish it was longer.<br /><br />I love seeing Kali being a badass. I mentioned in my review of the first book that Kali's greatness was more telling than showing and I'm so glad that isn't the case now. She's as fierce and as loyal as the first time I met her and I love her even more for it. I enjoyed seeing her relationship with Trace grow. I'm a huge romantic and I was scarily obsessed every time they're on a scene together. I got swept off my feet EVERY. TIME.<br /><br />I really do wish the book was longer. I felt like the ending was rushed a little too much. How everything wrapped up felt rather anticlimactic because of this. Or maybe that's just me wanting more of this duology. In which case I'm all for it. I would miss the rest of the gang too. Wil surprisingly grew on me. I love Luca and want more of him. I wish Leaf was more present in the story. I actually kind of like Raza. I really don't like him but Bahir was absent for most of the book considering he's the villain. I didn't feel like he's this powerful man whose putting people's lives at risk.<br /><br />Overall Unraveling Darkness was amazing! It was so much more than I expected and I loved it. And I'm still absolutely in love with Alex Lidell's writing.</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/6260635?shelf=arc-reads" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">arc-reads</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a hr