Id":35855553,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1510311895i/35855553._UX200_CR0,26,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":607,"textReviewsCount":5118,"name":"Siobhan","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/35855553-siobhan","contributor":null,"id":35855553},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1UZ3X4U45VYZL":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1UZ3X4U45VYZL"},"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.tm_O11-6QMM_lRTd-kKeBw":{"__typename":"Book","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.tm_O11-6QMM_lRTd-kKeBw"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1UZ3X4U45VYZL\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.tm_O11-6QMM_lRTd-kKeBw\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1UZ3X4U45VYZL","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1UZ3X4U45VYZL"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.tm_O11-6QMM_lRTd-kKeBw","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.tm_O11-6QMM_lRTd-kKeBw"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/35855553?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/2414569817"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.BlCQDV6XmkaNQys-oEx1mA":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.BlCQDV6XmkaNQys-oEx1mA","creator":{"__ref":"User:35855553"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1538329033080,"createdAt":1528237244892,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1528316402036,"text":"Being a big fan of Mulan since childhood, I always jump at any book that contains females pretending to be someone else to make it in a man’s world. Thus, I was instantly drawn towards Alex Lidell’s Scout duology. From the moment I read the synopsis of Tracing Shadows, I knew I needed to know more. I was more than happy to jump right in, and as soon as I was done I was left desperate for book two.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eUnraveling Darkness was a wonderful conclusion to the story, one I really enjoyed. It was not perfect, but I had so many feels moments throughout, powering through the book at a desperate rate to see how everything came together. There is no doubt I will be reading more Alex Lidell in the future, as Scout has confirmed the author sure knows how to pull me in with her fantasy worlds.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003ePicking up where Tracing Shadows ended, Unraveling Darkness throws us straight into the action. Things are moving from the very start, and do not let up throughout the book. Each chapter brings us something more, each throwing more towards us. There was so much to see, and Alex Lidell delivered so much throughout. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eOur characters continue to grow, giving us more of the wonderful interactions we came to enjoy in the first book. The romance was great, causing me to fall in deeper in love with the brewing relationship. The storyline was gripping, being fast paced and filled with everything to keep us turning the pages. The only thing I felt I would have liked more of was the world building. I really enjoyed the world building in the first book, but I do not feel as though it was as strong in this book. There was certainly a lot to see, but I feel as though some questions went unanswered. In some ways I would have liked this to be a trilogy, just so that I could better understand some aspects of the world, and why certain things played out the way they did. It wasn’t bad world building, far from it, it simply wasn’t the level I had hoped for considering everything that occurred throughout this one.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eWithout a doubt, I really enjoyed this conclusion to the Scout story. This was an insanely addictive duology, and I cannot wait to dive into more from the author.","rating":4,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1UZ3X4U45VYZL\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.tm_O11-6QMM_lRTd-kKeBw\"}}"},"likeCount":5,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:3533544":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":3533544,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1767332490i/3533544._UX200_CR0,39,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":110,"textReviewsCount":816,"name":"Hetal","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/3533544-hetal","contributor":null,"id":3533544},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1Z2V2J9WPGYGU":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1Z2V2J9WPGYGU"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1Z2V2J9WPGYGU\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.tm_O11-6QMM_lRTd-kKeBw\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1Z2V2J9WPGYGU","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1Z2V2J9WPGYGU"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.tm_O11-6QMM_lRTd-kKeBw","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.tm_O11-6QMM_lRTd-kKeBw"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/3533544?shelf=read"},"taggings":[{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"arcs","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/3533544?shelf=arcs"}}],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/2391008436"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.sgsWGHnKHJYt7Vgbjj4Zmg":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.sgsWGHnKHJYt7Vgbjj4Zmg","creator":{"__ref":"User:3533544"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1527887091993,"createdAt":1526558561750,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1526566481145,"text":"Received an ARC from the author. \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ebook 2 in the Scout duology was quite good. We catch up with Cali, Rune, Wil and their small team going to Rune's homeland in search of help for Dansil which has been taken over by the Goddess' messenger (AKA the high sparrow). \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e \u003cimg src=\"https://images.gr-assets.com/hostedimages/1526564988ra/25556773.gif\" class=\"gr-hostedUserImg\" loading=\"lazy\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eCali and Rune struggle to decide whether being together is not only the right choice for themselves, but all the right choices for their peoples. The romance was subtle yet sweet and you craved the moments they weren't fighting or trying to \"do the right thing.\"\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWil, while clearly scared, takes in stride his role and Dansil's new king. I liked that he didn't become high and mighty at the weight thrust upon his shoulders. He stayed the same silly Wil, just more jaded and serious in the face of politics.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eViolet as usual was just annoying an realized she f'ed up big time. Though, blessedly, her chapters were reduced in book 2. \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://images.gr-assets.com/hostedimages/1526565358ra/25556811.gif\" class=\"gr-hostedUserImg\" loading=\"lazy\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003ci\u003e [Violet's face when she realizes she just a pawn and has f***ed up big time] \u003c/i\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eAs for the plot and world building I'm sad to say it is largely undeveloped. What I expected to learn in book 2 about the world just never happened. The Eye (crystal) plot was poorly explained--and even after reading that part twice, I was still unsure of whether its role was good or evil. The magic structure with the use of crystals, whisperers, and mages was also not delved into nearly enough-in fact, barely at all. I don't think I fully understand their role.\u003cbr\u003e \u003cimg src=\"https://images.gr-assets.com/hostedimages/1479753941ra/21231890.gif\" class=\"gr-hostedUserImg\" loading=\"lazy\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e What does it mean for Cali to be the only other of her kind. Tell me more about the whisperers and their powers. What is the upkeep for keeping the crystal mines open and does Wil intend to re-cultivate the mining and go after Viva Sylthia for their cyrstals? What is the relationship between Wil's kingdom and Rune's kingdom at the end? \u003cbr\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://images.gr-assets.com/hostedimages/1513074787ra/24660091.gif\" class=\"gr-hostedUserImg\" loading=\"lazy\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe book leaves far too many open ended questions at the end. Enough so that I was left deeply unsatisfied with the ending. Is it a decent ending? Yes, definitely. But, Lidell leaves many plots untied with crystals, viva sylthia, toxic air(?), whisperers, relationships, and more. I felt vastly disappointed getting an abrupt ending that felt like it was rushed. If this was to be so, new plot points should not have been introduced. The whole mines of Viva Slythia thing could have been taken out, as could the strife with Rune's kingdom, his daddy issues, etc. \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eI'd like to take a moment to say that despite all the negatives, it still gets 3 stars because I did quite enjoy the journey. I enjoyed the trek through the forest and the witty banter between characters. I only wish this had been a trilogy to give Lidell the time she needed to develop the world, magic systems, and characters that grew and developed very little. She is far more than capable as seen in her Tildor books as well as her Tides series, if just given the proper time.","rating":3,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1Z2V2J9WPGYGU\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.tm_O11-6QMM_lRTd-kKeBw\"}}"},"likeCount":1,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:31792110":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":31792110,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1773790297i/31792110._UX200_CR0,33,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":3836,"textReviewsCount":1467,"name":"Namera [The Literary Invertebrate]","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/31792110-namera-the-literary-invertebrate","contributor":null,"id":31792110},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A278T7VEBDV3LT":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A278T7VEBDV3LT"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A278T7VEBDV3LT\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.tm_O11-6QMM_lRTd-kKeBw\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A278T7VEBDV3LT","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A278T7VEBDV3LT"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.tm_O11-6QMM_lRTd-kKeBw","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.tm_O11-6QMM_lRTd-kKeBw"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/31792110?shelf=read"},"taggings":[{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"genre-fantasy","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/31792110?shelf=genre-fantasy"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"genre-young-adult","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/31792110?shelf=genre-young-adult"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"arc","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/31792110?shelf=arc"}}],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/2392373040"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.HaT4qdtBuszoLMUWAqXqAA":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.HaT4qdtBuszoLMUWAqXqAA","creator":{"__ref":"User:31792110"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1526484233090,"createdAt":1526416013632,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1526416346948,"text":"Unravelling Darkness picks up immediately where Tracing Shadows ended, with our intrepid band travelling to Everett to seek shelter. As in the previous book, world-building is rather narrow, but the same certainly can't be said of the relationships - they, and the dash of romance, progress organically and believably. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI admit that I skimmed over most of the crystal and magic stuff because I just wasn't that interested, but that may well be just a 'me' issue. I also had to knock a star off because of Violet - no spoilers, but I felt so, so sorry for her! I do think the other characters, especially her own brother, ought to have shown a modicum more concern for her rather than just writing her off like that. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eOverall, a solid read with 4/5 stars for characters and 3 for plot. 3.5, here we come! ","rating":3,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A278T7VEBDV3LT\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.tm_O11-6QMM_lRTd-kKeBw\"}}"},"likeCount":1,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"Contributor:kca://author/amzn1.gr.author.v1.OIuc-riVi3PhqrD3e7lOZA":{"__typename":"Contributor","id":"kca://author/amzn1.gr.author.v1.OIuc-riVi3PhqrD3e7lOZA","works":{"__typename":"ContributorWorksConnection","totalCount":2}},"User:22943028":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":22943028,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1527895031i/22943028._UX200_CR0,25,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":true,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":28,"textReviewsCount":858,"name":"Lauralee","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/22943028-lauralee","contributor":{"__ref":"Contributor:kca://author/amzn1.gr.author.v1.OIuc-riVi3PhqrD3e7lOZA"},"id":22943028},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1902M92QBLVNH":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1902M92QBLVNH"},"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.uHSXpmpwprvjJ4VJJNbdYg":{"__typename":"Book","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.uHSXpmpwprvjJ4VJJNbdYg"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1902M92QBLVNH\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.uHSXpmpwprvjJ4VJJNbdYg\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1902M92QBLVNH","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1902M92QBLVNH"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.uHSXpmpwprvjJ4VJJNbdYg","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.uHSXpmpwprvjJ4VJJNbdYg"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/22943028?shelf=read"},"taggings":[{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"fantasy","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/22943028?shelf=fantasy"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"girls-disguised-as-boys","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/22943028?shelf=girls-disguised-as-boys"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"royalty","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/22943028?shelf=royalty"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"young-adult","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/22943028?shelf=young-adult"}}],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/2471630749"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.EtiHaEGq-1E8c5x9hKQ-7w":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.EtiHaEGq-1E8c5x9hKQ-7w","creator":{"__ref":"User:22943028"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1532652172367,"createdAt":1532652014397,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1532652172367,"text":"Kali, Trace, and the uncrowned king of Dansil is on the run. Bishop Bahir has seized the throne, and Kali’s sister is still imprisoned inside the palace. The only place for Kali and her gang to go is to Everett, their enemy kingdom. Once they arrive, Trace fights to keep his rightful inheritance, and Kali learns the truth about who she is. Can Kali save the kingdom of Dansil before it is too late?\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e Because I was so engaged in Kali’s character, I read this sequel in one sitting to find out what happened to her. Kali still has her spunkiness, but she has grown more mature. She is left with the impossible choice of leaving her sister behind. She has to make plans to restore her kingdom. This takes a burden on her. I was a bit disappointed that she was no longer a fighting warrior. Instead, she realizes that she has magical powers, and has to learn how to use them. Thus, Kali has become more mellow and grown up. I also thought that Kali’s relationship with Trace had deepened. They faced many obstacles and challenges, but they managed to overcome them.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e Overall, Unraveling Darkness is a coming of age novel about self-discovery. The novel emphasizes friendship, family, and sacrifice. I still thought that the supporting characters were not well-developed. For instance, I did not understand why Princess Raza hates Kali. The explanation seemed flimsy. The story seemed rushed in most parts. Trace’s background is barely explored with depth. There were also some scenes that I found uncomfortable. Despite these flaws, it was still an enjoyable and worthy sequel! Mrs. Liddell is a talented author, and I look forward to reading more of her series! This series is perfect for fans of Tamora Pierce, Rachel Hartman, and Sara B. Larson.","rating":4,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1902M92QBLVNH\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.uHSXpmpwprvjJ4VJJNbdYg\"}}"},"likeCount":0,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:6260635":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":6260635,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1735825909i/6260635._UX200_CR0,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":120,"textReviewsCount":935,"name":"diana","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/6260635-diana","contributor":null,"id":6260635},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A3IHE1BPAWD3WW":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A3IHE1BPAWD3WW"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A3IHE1BPAWD3WW\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.tm_O11-6QMM_lRTd-kKeBw\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A3IHE1BPAWD3WW","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A3IHE1BPAWD3WW"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.tm_O11-6QMM_lRTd-kKeBw","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.tm_O11-6QMM_lRTd-kKeBw"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/6260635?shelf=read"},"taggings":[{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"arc-reads","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/6260635?shelf=arc-reads"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"sent-by-author","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/6260635?shelf=sent-by-author"}}],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/2384195843"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.ZH2bUg9zO0HRAH2uHlHFFw":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.ZH2bUg9zO0HRAH2uHlHFFw","creator":{"__ref":"User:6260635"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1526452180792,"createdAt":1526450916903,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1526452180244,"text":"I can't believe it's done. This book was everything I hoped it would be. It was fast paced and thrilling with just the right amount of swoon to make my knees go weak. I took my time and savored every page. I didn't want it to end. I wish it was longer.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI love seeing Kali being a badass. I mentioned in my review of the first book that Kali's greatness was more telling than showing and I'm so glad that isn't the case now. She's as fierce and as loyal as the first time I met her and I love her even more for it. I enjoyed seeing her relationship with Trace grow. I'm a huge romantic and I was scarily obsessed every time they're on a scene together. I got swept off my feet EVERY. TIME.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI really do wish the book was longer. I felt like the ending was rushed a little too much. How everything wrapped up felt rather anticlimactic because of this. Or maybe that's just me wanting more of this duology. In which case I'm all for it. I would miss the rest of the gang too. Wil surprisingly grew on me. I love Luca and want more of him. I wish Leaf was more present in the story. I actually kind of like Raza. I really don't like him but Bahir was absent for most of the book considering he's the villain. I didn't feel like he's this powerful man whose putting people's lives at risk.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eOverall Unraveling Darkness was amazing! It was so much more than I expected and I loved it. And I'm still absolutely in love with Alex Lidell's writing.","rating":4,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A3IHE1BPAWD3WW\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.tm_O11-6QMM_lRTd-kKeBw\"}}"},"likeCount":0,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:43487600":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":43487600,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1540404648i/43487600._UX200_CR0,77,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":10,"textReviewsCount":38,"name":"Dakota","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/43487600-dakota","contributor":null,"id":43487600},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1V03NAH2N6QOK":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1V03NAH2N6QOK"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1V03NAH2N6QOK\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.tm_O11-6QMM_lRTd-kKeBw\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1V03NAH2N6QOK","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1V03NAH2N6QOK"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.tm_O11-6QMM_lRTd-kKeBw","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.tm_O11-6QMM_lRTd-kKeBw"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/43487600?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/2412647897"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.wIeCp-vhsrK62VvEd9BaPA":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.wIeCp-vhsrK62VvEd9BaPA","creator":{"__ref":"User:43487600"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1528088678465,"createdAt":1528087926408,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1528088677928,"text":"\u003cstrong\u003eSuperbly fantastic\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI cannot even begin to tell you how much I love this little series. I want more... No no correction I need more! I came across book one by happenstance and fell in love with Kali and Trace and Luca and wil! I love the strength and loyalty in them and book two only solidified and made me love it more if possible. This book makes me laugh, scream my frustrations and re-read a sentence multiple times because it is just that fantastic! \u003cbr /\u003eKali was a bit more vulnerable in this book than book one but I enjoyed it it was a good vulnerability . Don't get me wrong she is still BA but if you are fans of Trace you will love it all! \u003cbr /\u003eI'm hoping that there is a book three is in the works because there is still a few loose ends that need to be wrapped up. Certain apologies *ahem ahem* need to be made and if we are honest I just need more K and R!! \u003cbr /\u003eBrilliant series ( certain parts had me channeling princess bride), flowed perfectly, clenched my heart in my chest and had me squealing like a pig!! *wink wink* This book has me feeling so much I feel adrift now that it's over, whelp only thing left to do is re-read it all again!\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e","rating":5,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1V03NAH2N6QOK\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.tm_O11-6QMM_lRTd-kKeBw\"}}"},"likeCount":0,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:3710658":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":3710658,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1273528508i/3710658._UX200_CR0,34,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":58,"textReviewsCount":1379,"name":"Barbara","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/3710658-barbara","contributor":null,"id":3710658},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1OJBG9LF70X97":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1OJBG9LF70X97"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1OJBG9LF70X97\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.tm_O11-6QMM_lRTd-kKeBw\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1OJBG9LF70X97","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1OJBG9LF70X97"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.tm_O11-6QMM_lRTd-kKeBw","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.tm_O11-6QMM_lRTd-kKeBw"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/3710658?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/2388863374"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.2JWnKME1KVDXShWbNAedIQ":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.2JWnKME1KVDXShWbNAedIQ","creator":{"__ref":"User:3710658"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1528244963904,"createdAt":1528244951543,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1528244963288,"text":"Unraveling Darkness is the second book in the two book Scout series. It picks up right where Tracing Shadows left off, with Kali on the run with Trace, the young prince Wil, Luca and three others, after the King was killed and the kingdom taken over by mage and religious leader Bahir and his Holy Guard. The only place they can run to is Everett, the enemy kingdom they’ve been fighting with for years. The ragtag group seeks help from the Everett ruler, but his demands for assisting might be more than they are willing to pay. While Kali doesn’t have much time to master the new power she’s discovered within, she is determined to return to Dansil and rescue her sister Leaf, who was left behind when the group fled, no matter what it takes. Everyone must work together to make their plan to save the kingdom work, using all the skill, determination and courage they can muster. I loved all of the characters and their challenges, the love and camaraderie of most of the group, and the perseverance shown by them all. I’ve enjoyed other work by this author as well, and I can’t wait to read whatever else she comes up with.","rating":5,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1OJBG9LF70X97\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.tm_O11-6QMM_lRTd-kKeBw\"}}"},"likeCount":0,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:41889705":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":41889705,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1706375299i/41889705._UX200_CR0,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":4,"textReviewsCount":101,"name":"Cassie","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/41889705-cassie","contributor":null,"id":41889705},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A30F4B3JQ1320P":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A30F4B3JQ1320P"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A30F4B3JQ1320P\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.tm_O11-6QMM_lRTd-kKeBw\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A30F4B3JQ1320P","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A30F4B3JQ1320P"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.tm_O11-6QMM_lRTd-kKeBw","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.tm_O11-6QMM_lRTd-kKeBw"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/41889705?shelf=read"},"taggings":[{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"2018-books","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/41889705?shelf=2018-books"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"kindle-books","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/41889705?shelf=kindle-books"}}],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/2433187494"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.WZGgmi7AdedFgc_QxUJQew":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.WZGgmi7AdedFgc_QxUJQew","creator":{"__ref":"User:41889705"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1530850111401,"createdAt":1530849765131,"spoilerStatus":true,"lastRevisionAt":1530850110713,"text":"I enjoyed this second book much more than the first. While it was still fast paced, I feel like it was better written which allowed the story line to flow more easily between scenes. The twist with Kal’s power coming to light was awesome. I knew that there was something different with her but did not quite know what it was. Now the change in Trace/Rune’s demeanor towards everyone once he became the “prince” again was grating, particularly when enforcing the conservative women views. The entire trip to Everett that the group seemed to be pointless other than to discover Kal’s powers and further explain Rune’s backstory, and then the entire team returned to Delta, which is where all that forward movement could have happened. Anyway, I definitely found myself enjoying this second book so much more and I definitely appreciate having everything get nicely wrapped up. Even though this story ended, I feel like it leaves enough of an opportunity for Lindell to come back later and add to it if she would like. I personally would like to read more about the bond that Rube and Kal now have forged between them. ","rating":4,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A30F4B3JQ1320P\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.tm_O11-6QMM_lRTd-kKeBw\"}}"},"likeCount":0,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:33610461":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":33610461,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1535812619i/33610461._UX200_CR0,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":66,"textReviewsCount":3590,"name":"The Mysterious Reader","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/33610461-the-mysterious-reader","contributor":null,"id":33610461},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1P8R2KC1ZSF9S":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1P8R2KC1ZSF9S"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1P8R2KC1ZSF9S\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.tm_O11-6QMM_lRTd-kKeBw\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1P8R2KC1ZSF9S","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1P8R2KC1ZSF9S"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.tm_O11-6QMM_lRTd-kKeBw","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.tm_O11-6QMM_lRTd-kKeBw"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/33610461?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/2403061008"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.qYpCl-pmCluyf6MvjPCFpg":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.qYpCl-pmCluyf6MvjPCFpg","creator":{"__ref":"User:33610461"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1527307064562,"createdAt":1527307057038,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1527307063649,"text":"Ok, I will admit that I totally adore Alex Lidell’s novels. She is one of my absolute favorite authors and I’ve downloaded - and truly enjoyed - every single one of her novels to date. Her new Scout series is no exception and I was happy to give five stars to my review of its first book, Tracing Shadows. It’s no surprise then that I was delighted to get my hands on Unraveling Darkness, Book 2 of this series. It is also no surprise that this book is, quite simply, superb and definitely recommended. It had just what I wanted and was well written and with a great plot and great cast of characters. I frankly adore Kali and love watching Trace (Rune) and her take on all comers, and the rest of the cast of characters is pretty amazing as well. But for the fact that I’m literally dictating this review to my husband from my hospital bed I could go on and on with praises - the book definitely deserves it. Since I can’t do that I will simply note that the book is most definitely one to read, it is easy to highly recommend. I’m definitely looking forward to book 3.","rating":5,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1P8R2KC1ZSF9S\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.tm_O11-6QMM_lRTd-kKeBw\"}}"},"likeCount":0,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:7286511":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":7286511,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1565838300i/7286511._UX200_CR0